{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Rotational drivetrain",
  "exampleId": "block-drivetrain",
  "description": "A 1 N·m step at 0.1 s turns the motor inertia (0.01 kg·m²). The gear halves the speed and doubles the torque, the spring stands for shaft twist, and the load (0.04 kg·m²) spins against a 0.1 N·m·s damper. At steady state the load turns at 2 N·m / 0.1 = 20 rad/s, the motor at 40 rad/s, and 40 W flows through the shaft. The relative-speed sensor shows the shaft twisting back and forth before it settles.",
  "duration": 6,
  "revision": 0,
